  "summary": "I am a graduate and one time Instructor/Developer at devCodeCamp, where I built many projects and debugged many more.  Front-End, Back-End, I can build anything you need or integrate seamlessly with any team. \n\nExperience in many diverse tech stacks keeps me nimble and I'm eager to expand my knowledge to meet your unique requirements.\n\nI have done all kinds of work in many industries. I know the roles and rationale of nuclear reactor work, the features and of charcuterie of foundry & CNC, and have a sunny history in customer service. \n\nI can be a versatile member of any team, and am generally likable. I will solve your problems and produce clean, intuitive user interfaces and functional, secure back end services.",
